From: KConc competition team
Subject: [K11] Exclude complete x86 IDT asynchronous IRQ context from task KCOV

Based on Linux/MAccConc commit 2fc2e45b0cd75cd56f252a0872a6d039f46cc42b
with the accepted 0003 K10 control patch. This adds task-owned nesting around
the three asynchronous IDT wrappers; it does not filter recorded traces,
disable interrupts, change the delay budget, or modify synchronous exceptions.
CONFIG_X86_FRED and CONFIG_XEN must be disabled for the declared build scope.
The existing explicit remote-softirq exception is retained without extending
the supported execution model to nested remote/IRQ coverage.
License: GPL-2.0 (same as the modified Linux files).

